    <sys:String x:Key="LogBubbleDesc">2. BUBBLE (without Preview) - go from source to root</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LogDirectDesc">3. DIRECT - only on element, do not route</sys:String>

    <!-- Explanation text -->
    <sys:String x:Key="ExplanationTitle">=== ROUTING TYPES EXPLANATION ===</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TunnelingExplanation">1️⃣ TUNNELING (Preview* events):
   • Move TOP-DOWN (from root to source)
   • Example: Outer Border → Middle Border → Inner Border → Control
   • Used for preprocessing/interception</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="BubblingExplanation">2️⃣ BUBBLING (regular events):
   • Move BOTTOM-UP (from source to root)
   • Example: Control → Inner Border → Middle Border → Outer Border
   • Used for notifying parent elements</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="DirectExplanation">3️⃣ DIRECT events:
   • Processed ONLY on the source element
   • Do not go up or down the tree
   • Example: RatingConfirmed, QuantityConfirmed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SequenceExplanation">🔄 SEQUENCE when clicking on RatingControl:
1. TUNNEL: Outer Border (Preview) → Middle Border (Preview) → Control (Preview)
2. BUBBLE: Control (Changed) → Inner Border (Changed) → Middle Border (Changed) → Outer Border (Changed)
3. DIRECT (double-click): Only on control (Confirmed)</sys:String>
